  "confirm": {
    "Ask": {
      "title": "Apply “Like Garuda Linux (Dr460nized)”?",
      "text": "The look <b>Like Garuda Linux (Dr460nized)</b> will be applied to your desktop.<br><br>What will change: colours, Qt application style, GTK theme, icons, cursors, fonts, wallpaper.<br><br>Covered by the other parts: global theme — in Plasma it is one package of the parts listed here; on this desktop Rexon applies them one by one<br><br>Partly: colours — Qt programs pick it up after you log in again<br><br>Partly: Qt application style — Qt programs pick it up after you log in again<br><br>Rexon will install the programs it needs: qt6ct, kvantum, beautyline, ttf-fira-sans, ttf-firacode-nerd. Your system will ask for your password.<br><br>Won't be applied: window frames — Sway draws window borders itself, and there are no themes for them<br><br>Won't be applied: desktop shell theme — Sway has no shell theme of its own. If you use Noctalia or DankMaterialShell, press “Pass Palette to Shell” in Color Schemes after applying: they take the colours of this look<br><br>Won't be applied: panel layout — Sway has no panel of its own: a bar such as Waybar is chosen separately, in the Shells block of its card in Desktops<br><br>Won't be applied: desktop behaviour — it changes only things Plasma has: KWin window effects, the Plasma lock screen picture, KRunner in the middle of the screen — Sway has none of them<br><br>You can put everything back at any time with the “Put Back as It Was” button.",
      "yes_text": "Apply",
      "no_text": "Cancel",
      "choices": [],
      "option": null
    }
  },
